# herdr plugins, installed by setup.sh's `extensions` step.
#
# One owner/repo per line, as `herdr plugin install` takes it. `#` comments and
# blank lines are ignored.
#
# setup.sh installed two of these as literal command lines; three are installed
# on macbook-m5-pro. ogulcancelik/herdr-browser was the missing one, so a fresh
# machine silently came up without it.
#
# Note that the installed plugin id is not the repo name: herdr reports these as
# cloudmanic.herdr-plus, official.browser and tdi.worktree-setup respectively,
# which is why a directory listing under config/herdr/plugins/github/ cannot be
# used to reconstruct this list.

cloudmanic/herdr-plus
ogulcancelik/herdr-browser
tdi/herdr-worktree-setup
